# r521 template-maintenance/SKILL.md
SPLIT X:BF-L1-0139 | a@15-15: Place content by kind: normative constraint to a rule; multi-step procedure to a workflow skill; technique/examples to a knowledge skill or private reference; product facts to SPECIFICATION.md/CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md; mechanical check to a hook, script or configuration. | b@16-16: Place content by level, first match wins: project-specific selection/layout/default to 3-project; concrete non-platform technology to 2-technology; adopted architecture/role/boundary to 1-architecture; otherwise 0-core. | c@17-17: Content specific to a selected slot implementation goes into that module's facets and declares Capability; everything else uses roles and <slot>.<facet> references, never implementation names. | d@18-18: Always-needed planning policy goes into CLAUDE.md or an imported always rule; path-specific policy into a rule whose paths cover its scope; procedure obligations into the owning workflow. | e@19-19: Add each rule once; elsewhere use a pointer or a yes/no check naming the owner. | f@23-23: Keep the header line (Level, Capability when module-owned, Owns, Scope, Loading). | g@24-24: Update INSTRUCTION_MAP.md (level tables, capability view, policy locator). | h@26-26: Run check-instructions.mjs and fix every reported item.
